{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/922512-how-do-you-handle-xp-expenditure-learning-traits-during-gametime","id":922512,"title":"How do you handle XP expenditure/learning traits during gametime?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T02:15:09-07:00","id":922512,"title":"How do you handle XP expenditure/learning traits during gametime?","content":"This can be applied any of the gamlines so i put it here.<br /> <br /> If a player spends a part of a session having his character learn a new trait or expanding a trait how do you handle it? Lets say a character has a Discipline at 2 and wants to learn lvl 3 or wants to practice swordfighting.<br /> Do you allow them to try to use the new level at an increased difficulty (where applicable) or do handwave it as &quot;you spend the xp and suddenly you can use that level&quot;?<br /> How do you handle the situation where a player want's their character to learn a new level in a discipline/sphere/whatever but does not have the xp to spend right now? Sort of &quot;i want to practice the new level so that i can justify spending the xp on it afterwards&quot;<br /> <br /> Can you &quot;grind&quot; your way up to, for example, Presence 3 by using Presence 2 alot? Or by trying to use Presence 3 alot?<br /> <br /> Or do you just tell the player to wait until downtime to increase their stats?<br /> <br /> Mostly i feel that i comes down to two camp. One is &quot;The learning is a process that culminates in the expenditure of xp that represents what the character has learned during training&quot; and &quot;The xp expenditure signifies a sudden rush of insight that grants the character access to the knowledge of the new level&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T11:22:12-07:00","id":922747,"title":"","content":"I've usually ran it where they spend some of the time training, and so use the new dot level, but at a higher diff till they get a critical success (half or more of the dice rolled being successes) to show they have mastered it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:33:15-07:00","id":922940,"title":"","content":"Depends. Clan discipline can be bought any time. It's kind of a thicken of the blood and understanding the power of it. Blood magic has to be learned step by step except the primary path. Out of clan disciplines have to be tought and require at least a point of blood from the teacher except potence, celerity and fortitude. <br /> Abilities have either to be used in the game or trained in down time. <br /> Attributes fall in the middle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T18:11:29-07:00","id":924205,"title":"","content":"I just sort of dropped exp all together. Instead I have the player make &quot;Exp roles&quot;, when trying to upgrade a discipline/sphere/cantrip/regular skill etc.they have to use it out of combat and make a role for effect and another for &quot;Understanding&quot;. They role related attribute attribute(such as dexterity for dance or intelligence for thaumaturgy) + mentor background(if applicable, a sword instructor doesn't know a thing about magic), difficulty determined by what they wish to learn(so learning to bandage a wound at medicine 1 may be difficulty 5-6 while gaining the 5th dot and full mastery of the forces sphere would be difficulty 9-10). Each success gains the player 1 exp to be spent on the skill that was practiced(and that alone) botches remove 1 experience for each 1 rolled. Roles can only be made once a day.<br /> <br /> For things like garou gifts, they require a mentor(either another garou or a spirit), mentor background determined by the rank of said mentor. Attributes require you use said attribute(out of combat) and then role attribute + mentor(personal trainer, makeup artist, martial arts teacher, etc.) and certain attributes like appearance, intelligence, and perception can only be upgraded once in a play through without magical assistance(exception of vampires, once a night they can spend 1 BP and role said attribute for upgrade experience, cannot be done on the same night as any other experience roles. This is meant to represent the vampire gaining control over their undead form, like healing or blood buffing).<br /> <br /> Note: each exp role represents 1-8 hours of hard studying(based on what the player is trying to learn)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 06-30-2016, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}